Gitmore (https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gitmore.io) – natural language queries across GitHub, GitLab, and Bitbucket.<p>Instead of filtering PRs, scanning commit logs, or asking engineers for updates:<p>- &quot;What shipped last week?&quot;
- &quot;Who&#x27;s been working on the API?&quot;
- &quot;Which PRs have been open longest?&quot;
- &quot;Summarize this month&#x27;s releases&quot;<p>Plain English in, plain English out.<p>*How it works:*<p>Connect your repos via OAuth. We register webhooks. Every event gets normalized into a structured schema – commit message, PR description, author, timestamp, files changed.<p>The AI queries structured data, not raw text. PR descriptions and titles carry context that individual commits often miss.<p>*Automated reports:*<p>Don&#x27;t want to ask? Schedule it.<p>Weekly or monthly summaries delivered to Slack or email. Forward to stakeholders or let it run on autopilot.<p>*Other features:*
- Slack bot: Ask from where you already work
- Public changelog: yourcompany.gitmore.io&#x2F;changelog
- Contributor leaderboard<p>*Security:*<p>Metadata only. We store commit messages, PR titles, descriptions, timestamps, authors.<p>We never access source code, diffs, or file contents.<p>- Token encryption: Fernet (HMAC-SHA256 + AES-128-CBC)
- Webhook verification: HMAC-SHA256
- 2FA support<p>Verify yourself: check webhook settings after connecting.<p>Free for 1 repo: https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gitmore.io

I built One Card Tarot (<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;onecardtarot.org" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;onecardtarot.org</a>
), a simple web app that gives instant, one-card tarot readings with AI-generated interpretations.<p>The idea came from noticing that most tarot apps are either:<p>Overwhelming (full spreads, long rituals), or<p>Too generic (static meanings with no context)<p>I wanted something closer to how many people actually use tarot day to day:
ask one clear question, draw one card, and reflect.<p>What it does<p>Ask a question (or draw without one)<p>Draw one random tarot card (upright or reversed)<p>Get an AI-powered interpretation tailored to:<p>Love &amp; relationships<p>Yes &#x2F; No questions<p>Daily guidance &amp; reflection<p>Free users get limited daily readings, and there are optional paid plans for heavier use.<p>Why one card?<p>From my own experience, one-card tarot is:<p>Faster<p>Easier to reflect on<p>Less likely to turn into over-analysis<p>The constraint actually makes the interpretation more interesting.<p>Tech stack (high level)<p>Next.js<p>Serverless APIs<p>AI-generated interpretations (prompted to stay concise and grounded)<p>Stripe for payments<p>No accounts required to try it.<p>What I’m looking for<p>Feedback on the UX and interpretation quality<p>Thoughts on whether AI adds real value here or not<p>Suggestions for features that don’t make it more complicated<p>Happy to answer questions or share implementation details if useful.<p>Thanks!
